["city", "衣柜", "Your wardrobe", "Is your wardrobe full or almost empty?", "你的衣柜是满满的，还是几乎空的？", "Tell us about a piece of clothing with a story.", "讲讲一件有故事的衣服。", "When you moved here, what clothes did you have to buy? What did you bring that was useless?", "你搬到这里时，必须买哪些衣服？带来的哪些衣服没用？", "Some people wear the same outfit every day to save energy. Would you?", "有人为了节省精力每天穿同一套衣服。你会这样做吗？"],
["city", "快递", "Deliveries", "What was the last thing you ordered?", "你最近一次网购买了什么？", "Tell us about a delivery that went wrong.", "讲讲一次出了问题的快递。", "In China deliveries come in hours, in Germany often your neighbour takes your parcel. What surprised you about deliveries here?", "在中国，快递几个小时就到；在德国，常常是邻居帮你收包裹。这里的快递有什么让你惊讶？", "Fast delivery is convenient, but who pays the price: workers, the planet, local shops?", "快速配送很方便，但谁在付出代价：工人、地球，还是本地商店？"],
["city", "社区活动", "Neighbourhood events", "Have you been to a street party or neighbourhood festival?", "你参加过街坊聚会或社区节庆吗？", "Describe an event that brought your neighbours together.", "描述一个把邻居们聚在一起的活动。", "In Germany neighbours organise flea markets and street festivals, in Brazil \"festas juninas\", in China people dance in squares. What brings neighbours together where you come from?", "在德国，邻居们组织跳蚤市场和街道节；在巴西有“六月节”；在中国人们在广场跳舞。你家乡的邻居怎么聚到一起？", "Many people don't know their neighbours any more. How could we change that?", "很多人已经不认识自己的邻居了。我们怎样才能改变这一点？"],
["city", "散步", "Going for a walk", "Where do you usually walk?", "你通常在哪散步？", "Describe your favourite walk in your city.", "描述你在城市里最喜欢的散步路线。", "The Sunday walk is a German tradition. Do people walk \"just for fun\" where you come from?", "周日散步是德国的传统。在你的家乡，人们会“只为了散步而散步”吗？", "Many writers and thinkers walked to find ideas. Why does walking help us think?", "许多作家和思想家靠散步寻找灵感。为什么散步能帮助思考？"],
["city", "夜生活", "Nightlife", "Bar, club, karaoke or a quiet restaurant?", "酒吧、夜店、KTV还是安静的餐厅？", "Describe a great night out you remember.", "描述一个你记得的精彩夜晚。", "Berlin clubs open until Monday, Chinese night markets go until late, Brazilian parties start at midnight. How is nightlife where you come from?", "柏林的夜店开到周一，中国的夜市开到很晚，巴西的派对半夜才开始。你家乡的夜生活是怎样的？", "Does nightlife change as we get older? What do you enjoy now that you didn't before?", "夜生活会随着年龄改变吗？你现在喜欢哪些以前不喜欢的？"],
["city", "城市的声音", "Sounds of the city", "Is your street noisy or quiet?", "你住的街吵还是安静？", "Describe the sounds of your hometown: morning, afternoon and night.", "描述你家乡的声音：早晨、下午和夜晚。", "Church bells in Germany, street sellers in China, music in Brazil: which city sound do you miss most?", "德国的教堂钟声、中国的街头叫卖、巴西的音乐：你最怀念哪种城市的声音？", "Noise can make people ill, but total silence can feel strange too. What is the right amount of sound for you?", "噪音会让人生病，可是完全安静也会让人觉得奇怪。对你来说多少声音刚刚好？"],
["city", "河边", "By the river", "What do people do by the river?", "人们在河边做什么？", "Describe a river you love, here or in your hometown.", "描述一条你喜爱的河，在这里或你的家乡。", "The Rhine, the Yangtze, the Amazon: why did so many cities grow up next to rivers?", "莱茵河、长江、亚马孙河：为什么那么多城市沿河而建？", "Some cities have cleaned their rivers so people can swim again. Should every city do this?", "一些城市把河治理干净了，人们又能游泳了。每座城市都该这样做吗？"],
["city", "停电", "Power cut", "What would you do tonight if the power went out?", "如果今晚停电了，你会做什么？", "Tell us about a power cut you remember. What did people do?", "讲讲一次你记得的停电。大家都做了什么？", "In some places power cuts are normal, in Germany they are rare. How does that change how people prepare?", "在有些地方停电很平常，在德国却很少见。这会怎样影响人们的准备？", "Sometimes a power cut brings neighbours together. Why do we need a small crisis to talk to each other?", "有时一次停电能把邻居们聚到一起。为什么我们需要一点小危机才会彼此交谈？"],
["city", "在电梯里", "In the lift", "Do you talk to people in the lift?", "你在电梯里和别人说话吗？", "Tell us about a funny or awkward moment in a lift.", "讲讲在电梯里一个好笑或尴尬的时刻。", "Why do people look at the floor numbers or their phones in a lift?", "为什么人们在电梯里都盯着楼层数字或手机？", "If you had 30 seconds in a lift with someone important, what would you say?", "如果你和一位重要人物在电梯里有三十秒，你会说什么？"],
["city", "熟悉的面孔", "Familiar faces", "Do you greet people you don't really know?", "你会和不太认识的人打招呼吗？", "Tell us about a \"familiar stranger\": the bus driver, a dog walker, the man at the kiosk.", "讲讲一个“熟悉的陌生人”：公交司机、遛狗的人、报亭的大叔。", "Would you notice if one of these familiar faces suddenly disappeared? Would you worry?", "如果其中一张熟悉的面孔突然不见了，你会注意到吗？会担心吗？", "Small daily contacts make us feel part of a place. Why are they so important?", "日常的小小接触让我们感到自己属于一个地方。为什么它们如此重要？"],
["city", "城市地标", "City landmarks", "Have you been to the top of a famous tower?", "你登上过著名的塔顶吗？", "Describe a landmark from your hometown that you are proud of.", "描述一个让你骄傲的家乡地标。", "The Brandenburg Gate, the Oriental Pearl Tower, Christ the Redeemer: what makes a building a symbol of a city?", "勃兰登堡门、东方明珠、基督像：是什么让一座建筑成为城市的象征？", "Locals often never visit their own landmarks. Why? Have you visited yours?", "本地人常常从不去自己城市的地标。为什么？你去过自己城市的吗？"],
["city", "下雨天", "Rainy days", "What do you do when it rains all day?", "整天下雨时你做什么？", "Tell us about a time you got completely wet in the rain.", "讲讲一次你被雨淋得透湿的经历。", "Germans say \"there is no bad weather, only the wrong clothes\". Do you agree?", "德国人说“没有坏天气，只有穿错的衣服”。你同意吗？", "Rain can make people sad, but some people love it. Why does weather affect us so differently?", "下雨会让人难过，但也有人很喜欢。为什么天气对每个人的影响如此不同？"],
["city", "夜景", "City lights at night", "Where is the best place to see your city at night?", "在哪里看你城市的夜景最好？", "Describe the most beautiful night view you have ever seen.", "描述你见过的最美的夜景。", "Shanghai's Bund, Rio from Sugarloaf, Hamburg's harbour: what makes a night view unforgettable?", "上海外滩、面包山上的里约、汉堡港：是什么让一处夜景难忘？", "Bright cities hide the stars. Is light pollution a real problem?", "明亮的城市遮住了星星。光污染是个真正的问题吗？"],
["city", "厨房", "The kitchen", "What is your favourite thing in your kitchen?", "你厨房里最喜欢的东西是什么？", "Describe your family's kitchen when you were a child.", "描述一下你小时候家里的厨房。", "Why do parties always end up in the kitchen?", "为什么派对最后总是聚在厨房里？", "Is the kitchen the real heart of a home? What happens there that doesn't happen anywhere else?", "厨房是家真正的心脏吗？那里会发生哪些在别处不会发生的事？"],
["city", "阳台", "The balcony", "What do you do on your balcony?", "你在阳台上做什么？", "Describe your dream balcony.", "描述你梦想中的阳台。", "In China balconies are often closed with glass, in Germany they are open and full of flowers. Why the difference?", "在中国，阳台常常用玻璃封起来；在德国，阳台是开放的，摆满了花。为什么会有这种差别？", "During lockdowns people sang and talked from balconies. What can a balcony give us?", "居家隔离期间，人们在阳台上唱歌、聊天。阳台能给我们什么？"],
["city", "窗外的风景", "The view from your window", "Do you like your view? Why or why not?", "你喜欢你窗外的景色吗？为什么？", "Describe the view from your childhood bedroom.", "描述你小时候卧室窗外的景色。", "Would you pay more rent for a beautiful view? How much is a view worth?", "你会为了美景多付房租吗？一扇窗外的风景值多少钱？", "Watching the same view every day, you see small changes. What have you noticed over time?", "每天看同一片风景，你会看到细微的变化。随着时间推移，你注意到了什么？"],
["city", "泡澡还是淋浴", "Bath or shower", "Do you shower in the morning or in the evening?", "你早上洗澡还是晚上洗澡？", "Tell us about a special bath: a hot spring, a sauna or a public bath.", "讲讲一次特别的沐浴经历：温泉、桑拿或澡堂。", "Brazilians often shower twice a day, Germans save water, Chinese northern bathhouses are social places. How is it where you come from?", "巴西人常常一天洗两次澡，德国人节约用水，中国北方的澡堂是社交场所。你家乡是怎样的？", "Many people get their best ideas in the shower. Why?", "很多人在洗澡时会冒出最好的点子。为什么？"],
["city", "钥匙", "Keys", "Have you ever locked yourself out?", "你有没有把自己锁在门外过？", "Tell us the story of a time you lost your keys.", "讲讲你丢钥匙的一次经历。", "In Germany a locksmith can cost hundreds of euros, so many people leave a key with a neighbour. Who has your spare key?", "在德国请开锁匠可能要几百欧，所以很多人把备用钥匙放在邻居那。谁有你的备用钥匙？", "Giving someone your key is a sign of trust. Who would you trust with your home?", "把钥匙交给别人是一种信任。你会把家托付给谁？"],
["city", "垃圾分类", "Sorting rubbish", "How many bins do you have at home?", "你家里有几个垃圾桶？", "Tell us about your first experience with German rubbish rules.", "讲讲你第一次接触德国垃圾分类规则的经历。", "Germany has many bins and a bottle deposit, Shanghai started strict rules in 2019. How is it where you come from?", "德国有很多种垃圾桶和瓶子押金制度，上海2019年开始实行严格的规定。你家乡是怎样的？", "Is sorting rubbish really helpful, or should companies make less packaging instead?", "垃圾分类真的有用吗？还是企业应该少做包装？"],
["city", "家规", "House rules", "Do you take your shoes off at home?", "你在家脱鞋吗？", "Tell us about a strange house rule from your childhood.", "讲讲你小时候家里一条奇怪的规矩。", "German buildings have \"quiet hours\" when you shouldn't drill or play loud music. Is there something similar where you come from?", "德国的楼房有“安静时间”，那时候不能钻墙或大声放音乐。你的家乡有类似的规定吗？", "Which rules make living together easier, and which just cause arguments?", "哪些规矩让一起生活更容易，哪些只会引起争吵？"],
["city", "在城里开车", "Driving in the city", "What is the hardest thing about driving here?", "在这里开车最难的是什么？", "Tell us about a funny or stressful parking story.", "讲讲一次有趣或让人抓狂的停车经历。", "German drivers follow rules strictly, in some cities drivers honk all the time. How would you describe drivers where you come from?", "德国司机严格守规矩，有些城市的司机一直按喇叭。你会怎么形容你家乡的司机？", "Should city centres be closed to private cars? What would we gain and lose?", "市中心应该禁止私家车进入吗？我们会得到什么、失去什么？"],
["city", "节约能源", "Saving energy", "What do you do to save energy at home?", "你在家做什么来节约能源？", "Tell us about a time energy prices changed your habits.", "讲讲一次能源价格改变了你习惯的经历。", "In Germany people open windows wide for five minutes instead of keeping them half open. Have you learned habits like this?", "在德国，人们把窗户大开五分钟，而不是一直半开着。你学到过类似的习惯吗？", "Can small habits at home really make a difference, or do we need bigger changes?", "家里的小习惯真的能带来改变吗？还是我们需要更大的变革？"],
["city", "城市里的动物", "City animals", "Are there many dogs in your neighbourhood?", "你住的地方狗多吗？", "Tell us about a surprising animal you met in the city.", "讲讲你在城市里遇到的一只令人惊讶的动物。", "Foxes in Berlin, monkeys in Rio, cats in Chinese alleys: how do wild animals live in cities?", "柏林的狐狸、里约的猴子、中国胡同里的猫：野生动物怎样在城市里生存？", "Should cities be designed for animals too? How?", "城市也应该为动物而设计吗？怎样设计？"],
["city", "健身房", "The gym", "What do you do there: weights, running, classes?", "你在那里做什么：举铁、跑步还是上课？", "Tell us about a funny or embarrassing moment at the gym.", "讲讲你在健身房遇到的有趣或尴尬的事。", "Many people buy a membership in January and never go. Why?", "很多人一月份办了健身卡就再也没去过。为什么？", "Is exercise better alone or with others? What keeps you motivated?", "运动是一个人好，还是和别人一起好？什么让你保持动力？"],
["city", "公共厕所", "Public toilets", "Do you have to pay for toilets here?", "在这里上厕所要付钱吗？", "Tell us about the strangest or best toilet you have ever seen.", "讲讲你见过的最奇怪或最好的厕所。", "Japanese toilets are high-tech, German toilets often cost 50 cents, Chinese cities built many new public toilets. What surprised you abroad?", "日本的马桶很高科技，德国的厕所常要五十分，中国城市新建了很多公厕。在国外什么让你惊讶？", "Should public toilets be free? Who should pay for them?", "公共厕所应该免费吗？应该由谁来付钱？"],
["city", "你住的那条街", "Your street", "What shops or places are on your street?", "你住的街上有什么商店或地方？", "Describe your street on a Saturday morning.", "描述一下星期六早上你住的那条街。", "Many German streets are named after poets, Chinese streets after cities, Brazilian streets after dates. Who or what is your street named after?", "很多德国街道以诗人命名，中国街道以城市命名，巴西街道以日期命名。你住的街以谁或什么命名？", "If you could change one thing about your street, what would it be?", "如果你能改变你住的街上的一样东西，会是什么？"],
["city", "城市热浪", "Heatwaves in the city", "Do you have air conditioning at home?", "你家里有空调吗？", "Tell us about the hottest day you remember.", "讲讲你记得的最热的一天。", "Most German homes have no air conditioning, while in China and Brazil it is normal. How do people deal with heat where you come from?", "大多数德国家庭没有空调，而在中国和巴西空调很普遍。你家乡的人怎么应对炎热？", "Summers are getting hotter. How should cities change: more trees, more fountains, more shade?", "夏天越来越热。城市应该怎样改变：更多的树、更多的喷泉、更多的阴凉？"],
["lang", "方言", "Dialects", "What is a word in your dialect that others don't understand?", "你方言里有什么词是别人听不懂的？", "Tell us about a time you couldn't understand someone's dialect.", "讲讲一次你听不懂别人方言的经历。", "Bavarian, Cantonese, the accent from Bahia: why do dialects make people feel at home?", "巴伐利亚话、粤语、巴伊亚口音：为什么方言让人有家的感觉？", "Many young people no longer speak their grandparents' dialect. Should we try to save dialects?", "很多年轻人已经不会说祖辈的方言了。我们应该努力保护方言吗？"],
["lang", "俚语", "Slang", "Teach us one slang word from your language.", "教我们一个你语言里的俚语。", "Tell us about a slang word you used wrong, or that confused you.", "讲讲一个你用错或让你困惑的俚语。", "\"Krass\" in German, \"legal\" in Brazilian Portuguese, \"牛\" in Chinese: why does every language need words for \"cool\"?", "德语的“krass”、巴西葡语的“legal”、中文的“牛”：为什么每种语言都需要表示“酷”的词？", "Slang changes fast. Is it good for language learners to learn it, or is it better to avoid it?", "俚语变化很快。语言学习者学它好，还是避开更好？"],
["lang", "动物俗语", "Animal sayings", "Which animal appears in many sayings in your language?", "在你的语言里，哪种动物出现在很多俗语中？", "Explain a funny animal saying from your language.", "解释一句你语言里有趣的动物俗语。", "Germans have a \"pig\" for luck, Chinese \"draw a snake and add feet\", Brazilians \"pay the duck\". Why are animals so useful in language?", "德国人说“有猪”表示走运，中国人说“画蛇添足”，巴西人说“替鸭子付钱”。为什么动物在语言中那么好用？", "Do animal sayings show how a culture sees animals? Give an example.", "动物俗语能看出一种文化怎么看待动物吗？举个例子。"],
["lang", "外语糗事", "Language mistakes", "Which word do you always mix up?", "你总是搞混哪个词？", "Tell us your most embarrassing language mistake.", "讲讲你最尴尬的一次语言失误。", "\"Ich bin heiß\" instead of \"Mir ist heiß\" is a classic German mistake. What classic mistakes do learners make in your language?", "说“Ich bin heiß”（我很性感）而不是“Mir ist heiß”（我很热）是德语经典错误。学你母语的人常犯哪些经典错误？", "Are mistakes the best way to learn? Why are we so afraid of them?", "犯错是最好的学习方式吗？我们为什么那么害怕犯错？"],
["lang", "最难发的音", "The hardest sound", "Can you say \"Eichhörnchen\" or \"Brötchen\"?", "你会说“Eichhörnchen”或“Brötchen”吗？", "Teach us a sound from your language that is hard for others.", "教我们一个你语言里别人觉得很难的音。", "Chinese has tones, German has \"ü\" and \"ch\", Portuguese has nasal sounds. Which language is hardest to pronounce for you?", "中文有声调，德语有“ü”和“ch”，葡萄牙语有鼻音。对你来说哪种语言最难发音？", "Can adults ever lose their accent completely? Should they want to?", "成年人能完全去掉口音吗？他们应该想去掉吗？"],
["lang", "绕口令", "Tongue twisters", "Say a tongue twister from your language. Can others repeat it?", "说一个你语言里的绕口令。别人能跟着说吗？", "\"Fischers Fritz fischt frische Fische\", \"吃葡萄不吐葡萄皮\", \"O rato roeu a roupa do rei de Roma\": which is the hardest?", "“Fischers Fritz fischt frische Fische”、“吃葡萄不吐葡萄皮”、“O rato roeu a roupa do rei de Roma”：哪个最难？", "Why are tongue twisters so funny when we make mistakes?", "为什么我们说错绕口令时会那么好笑？", "Can tongue twisters really help us learn pronunciation? How?", "绕口令真的能帮助我们学发音吗？怎么帮？"],
["lang", "最美的词", "The most beautiful word", "Which word in another language sounds beautiful to you?", "哪种外语里的哪个词你觉得很好听？", "Tell us about a word that has a special meaning for you.", "讲讲一个对你有特殊意义的词。", "Is a word beautiful because of its sound or its meaning?", "一个词美，是因为它的发音，还是它的意思？", "Germans once voted \"Habseligkeiten\" (belongings) the most beautiful German word. What word would you vote for in your language, and why?", "德国人曾票选“Habseligkeiten”（随身物品）为最美德语词。你会为自己语言里的哪个词投票？为什么？"],
["lang", "无法翻译的词", "Untranslatable words", "Which word from your language do you miss when you speak another?", "说别的语言时，你会想念母语里哪个词？", "Explain a word from your language that is hard to translate.", "解释一个你语言里很难翻译的词。", "\"Saudade\", \"Feierabend\", \"缘分\": what do these words tell us about each culture?", "“Saudade”、“Feierabend”、“缘分”：这些词告诉了我们各个文化的什么？", "If a language has no word for a feeling, can people still feel it?", "如果一种语言没有描述某种感受的词，人们还能感受到它吗？"],
["lang", "外来词", "Loanwords", "Do you know a German word in another language?", "你知道别的语言里有哪个德语词吗？", "Tell us a loanword in your language that surprised you.", "讲讲一个让你惊讶的母语里的外来词。", "\"Kindergarten\" went into English, \"沙发\" came from \"sofa\", \"Handy\" is German for a phone. Why do languages borrow words?", "“Kindergarten”进入了英语，“沙发”来自“sofa”，“Handy”在德语里指手机。语言为什么会借词？", "Some people want to protect their language from English words. Is that a good idea?", "有人想保护自己的语言不受英语词影响。这是个好主意吗？"],
["lang", "品牌名翻译", "Brand names in translation", "How do people in your country pronounce foreign brands?", "你们国家的人怎么念外国品牌？", "Tell us a funny or clever brand name translation.", "讲一个有趣或巧妙的品牌名翻译。", "\"可口可乐\" means \"tasty and fun\", \"宝马\" means \"precious horse\". Why do brands choose names with meanings in Chinese?", "“可口可乐”意思是“好喝又快乐”，“宝马”意思是“宝贵的马”。为什么品牌在中文里要选有含义的名字？", "Some brand names sound bad in other languages. How careful should companies be?", "有些品牌名在别的语言里听起来很糟。公司应该多小心？"],
["lang", "网络用语", "Internet language", "What does \"LOL\", \"666\" or \"kkkkk\" mean?", "“LOL”、“666”或“kkkkk”是什么意思？", "Explain an internet word from your language that your parents don't understand.", "解释一个你父母听不懂的母语网络用语。", "Brazilians laugh \"kkkkk\", Chinese laugh \"哈哈哈\", Germans laugh \"haha\". How do people laugh in writing in different languages?", "巴西人写“kkkkk”，中国人写“哈哈哈”，德国人写“haha”。不同语言的人怎么用文字笑？", "Is internet language making our language poorer, or richer?", "网络用语让我们的语言更贫乏了，还是更丰富了？"],
["lang", "拟声词", "Sound words", "What sound does a cat, a cow or a rooster make in your language?", "在你的语言里猫、牛或公鸡怎么叫？", "Compare sound words for sneezing, knocking or eating in different languages.", "比较不同语言里打喷嚏、敲门或吃东西的拟声词。", "A German rooster says \"kikeriki\", a Chinese one \"喔喔喔\", a Brazilian one \"cocoricó\". Why do animals \"speak\" differently in each language?", "德国公鸡叫“kikeriki”，中国公鸡叫“喔喔喔”，巴西公鸡叫“cocoricó”。为什么动物在每种语言里“说”得不一样？", "Comics use many sound words: \"boom\", \"bang\", \"zack\". Which language has the best sound words?", "漫画里用很多拟声词：“砰”、“嘭”、“咔嚓”。哪种语言的拟声词最好？"],
["lang", "数数", "Counting", "How do you show numbers with your fingers?", "你怎么用手指表示数字？", "In which language do you count and do maths in your head?", "你心算时用哪种语言？", "Germans say \"four-and-twenty\" for 24, Chinese show 6 with thumb and little finger. What confused you about numbers abroad?", "德国人把24说成“四和二十”，中国人用拇指和小指比6。在国外，数字的什么让你困惑？", "Many bilingual people always count in their first language. Why are numbers so deep in us?", "许多双语者总是用母语数数。为什么数字在我们心里扎得那么深？"],
["lang", "称呼", "Forms of address", "How do you address your boss or teacher?", "你怎么称呼你的老板或老师？", "Tell us about a time you used the wrong form of address.", "讲讲一次你用错称呼的经历。", "Chinese has \"哥\", \"姐\", \"阿姨\" for strangers, German has \"du\" and \"Sie\", Portuguese has \"você\" and \"o senhor\". What do these words tell us about relationships?", "中文用“哥”、“姐”、“阿姨”称呼陌生人，德语有“du”和“Sie”，葡萄牙语有“você”和“o senhor”。这些词反映了怎样的人际关系？", "Is the move from \"Sie\" to \"du\" a big moment? Who should offer it first?", "从“Sie”改成“du”是个重要时刻吗？应该由谁先提出？"],
["lang", "手势", "Gestures", "Show us a gesture from your country. What does it mean?", "给我们比一个你们国家的手势。它是什么意思？", "Tell us about a gesture that caused a misunderstanding.", "讲讲一个引起误会的手势。", "The \"OK\" sign is positive in Germany, rude in Brazil. Chinese people beckon with the palm down. Which gestures should travellers know?", "“OK”手势在德国是正面的，在巴西却不礼貌。中国人招手时掌心朝下。旅行者应该知道哪些手势？", "Can we understand each other with gestures only? How much of communication is the body?", "我们能只靠手势互相理解吗？沟通中有多少是靠身体？"],
["lang", "口头禅", "Catchphrases", "What does your mum or dad always say?", "你妈妈或爸爸总说什么？", "Ask the people here: what is my catchphrase?", "问问在座的人：我的口头禅是什么？", "\"Genau\", \"就是\", \"tipo assim\": which filler words do you use in each language?", "“Genau”、“就是”、“tipo assim”：你在每种语言里用什么口头语？", "When you learn a language, do you pick up other people's catchphrases? Does it change how you speak?", "学语言时，你会学到别人的口头禅吗？它会改变你说话的方式吗？"],
["lang", "打字和输入法", "Typing and input methods", "How do you type Chinese, German umlauts or Portuguese accents?", "你怎么打中文、德语变元音或葡萄牙语的重音符号？", "Tell us about a funny autocorrect mistake.", "讲讲一次好笑的自动纠错错误。", "Many Chinese people type pinyin and forget how to write characters by hand. Has typing changed how you write?", "很多中国人用拼音打字，忘了怎么手写汉字。打字改变了你写字的方式吗？", "Voice messages, typing, handwriting: which will survive in 50 years?", "语音消息、打字、手写：五十年后哪种还会存在？"],
["lang", "汉字和字母", "Characters and letters", "What is your favourite Chinese character or letter? Why?", "你最喜欢哪个汉字或字母？为什么？", "Explain how a Chinese character is built, or teach us one.", "解释一个汉字是怎么构成的，或者教我们一个。", "Chinese uses thousands of characters, German 30 letters, Portuguese has many accents. Which is hardest to learn?", "中文要用几千个汉字，德语有30个字母，葡萄牙语有很多重音符号。哪个最难学？", "Does a writing system change how people think?", "一种文字系统会改变人们的思维方式吗？"],
["lang", "双关语", "Puns", "Tell us a pun in your language. Can you explain it?", "说一个你语言里的双关语。你能解释吗？", "Chinese New Year uses many puns: fish (鱼) sounds like \"surplus\" (余). Do you know others?", "春节有很多谐音：鱼听起来像“余”。你还知道其他的吗？", "German hairdressers love puns: \"Haarmonie\", \"Vorhair Nachhair\". Why do shops use puns in their names?", "德国理发店很爱用双关语：“Haarmonie”、“Vorhair Nachhair”。商店为什么喜欢在店名里用双关？", "Is understanding puns the final test of knowing a language?", "听懂双关语是掌握一门语言的终极考验吗？"],
["lang", "冷笑话", "Bad jokes", "Tell us your best (or worst) joke.", "讲讲你最好（或最烂）的笑话。", "Who in your family tells the worst jokes?", "你家里谁讲的笑话最冷？", "Some jokes only work in one language. Translate a joke from your language and see if it survives.", "有些笑话只在一种语言里好笑。翻译一个你语言里的笑话，看它还好不好笑。", "Why do we laugh at jokes that are so bad? What makes something funny?", "为什么我们会被那么烂的笑话逗笑？什么让一件事变得好笑？"],
["lang", "菠萝披萨", "Pineapple on pizza", "What is the strangest pizza you have eaten?", "你吃过最奇怪的披萨是什么？", "Brazilians put chocolate or corn on pizza, Germans put tuna. Defend your favourite strange topping!", "巴西人在披萨上放巧克力或玉米，德国人放金枪鱼。为你最喜欢的奇怪配料辩护吧！", "When food travels to another country, does it have to stay \"authentic\"?", "食物传到另一个国家时，必须保持“正宗”吗？", "Why do people argue so passionately about food? What is really at stake?", "为什么人们为了食物争得那么激烈？真正的分歧在哪里？"],
["lang", "先有鸡还是先有蛋", "Chicken or egg?", "Do you like questions with no answer?", "你喜欢没有答案的问题吗？", "Share another \"impossible\" question you have thought about.", "分享另一个你思考过的“无解”问题。", "Some cultures love debating, others avoid it. How do people discuss unanswerable questions where you come from?", "有些文化喜欢辩论，有些文化回避辩论。你家乡的人怎么讨论没有答案的问题？", "Why do humans love questions that can never be answered?", "人类为什么喜欢永远没有答案的问题？"],
["lang", "牙膏怎么挤", "How do you squeeze toothpaste?", "Toilet paper: over or under?", "卫生纸：外挂还是里挂？", "Tell us about a small habit that started a big argument at home.", "讲讲一个在家里引发大争吵的小习惯。", "Why do tiny habits annoy us so much in people we live with?", "为什么同住的人的小习惯会让我们那么恼火？", "Is there a \"right\" way to do everyday things, or is it just what we grew up with?", "日常小事有“正确”的做法吗？还是只是我们从小习惯的方式？"],
["lang", "打电话还是发消息", "Call or text?", "When was the last time you called a friend just to talk?", "你上次只是为了聊天给朋友打电话是什么时候？", "Tell us about a misunderstanding that happened because of a text message.", "讲讲一次因为短信引起的误会。", "Many young people are nervous about phone calls. Why?", "很多年轻人害怕打电话。为什么？", "Is talking on the phone in a foreign language harder than talking face to face? Why?", "用外语打电话比面对面说话更难吗？为什么？"],
["lang", "谜语", "Riddles", "Tell us a riddle from your childhood.", "讲一个你小时候的谜语。", "\"The more you take, the more you leave behind. What am I?\" Can you solve it? Make your own riddle.", "“你拿得越多，留下的就越多。我是什么？”你能猜出来吗？编一个你自己的谜语。", "Chinese lantern riddles often play with characters. How do riddles work in your language?", "中国的灯谜常常玩汉字。你语言里的谜语是怎么玩的？", "Why do riddles exist in every culture? What do they train?", "为什么每种文化都有谜语？它们锻炼的是什么？"],
["lang", "文字游戏", "Word games", "Scrabble, Wordle, crosswords or word chains: which do you like?", "拼字游戏、Wordle、填字还是词语接龙：你喜欢哪个？", "Let's play now: say a word, the next person says a word starting with the last letter!", "现在就来玩：说一个词，下一个人用最后一个字母开头说一个词！", "In China people play \"idiom chains\" where each idiom starts with the last character of the one before. What word games are popular where you come from?", "中国人玩“成语接龙”，每个成语都用上一个的最后一个字开头。你家乡流行什么文字游戏？", "Are word games a good way to learn a language? Why?", "文字游戏是学语言的好方法吗？为什么？"],
["lang", "成语", "Chinese idioms", "What is your favourite idiom or saying in any language?", "在任何语言里，你最喜欢的成语或俗语是什么？", "Explain the story behind an idiom, like \"对牛弹琴\" (playing the lute to a cow).", "讲讲一个成语背后的故事，比如“对牛弹琴”。", "Many Chinese idioms have four characters and a story from history. Does your language have sayings with stories behind them?", "很多成语有四个字，背后都有历史故事。你的语言里也有背后有故事的俗语吗？", "Is it important for learners to know idioms, or is it better to speak simply?", "学习者知道成语重要吗？还是说简单点更好？"],
["lang", "听错的歌词", "Misheard lyrics", "Which foreign song did you sing as a child without understanding?", "小时候你唱过哪首听不懂的外语歌？", "Tell us about the funniest lyrics you misheard.", "讲讲你听错过的最好笑的歌词。", "In Germany misheard lyrics are called \"Verhörer\" and there are whole books of them. Why do our brains make up words?", "在德国，听错的歌词叫“Verhörer”，有整本书收集它们。我们的大脑为什么会自己编词？", "Does it matter if we don't understand a song's words? Can we still feel the song?", "听不懂歌词要紧吗？我们还能感受到这首歌吗？"],
["lang", "翻译的片名", "Translated film titles", "Do you know a film whose title is very different in your language?", "你知道哪部电影在你语言里的片名差别很大吗？", "Tell us a funny or strange translated film title.", "讲一个好笑或奇怪的翻译片名。", "German titles often add an English subtitle, Chinese titles sometimes explain the whole story. Why do translators change titles so much?", "德语片名常加个英文副标题，中文片名有时会把整个故事讲出来。译者为什么要大改片名？", "Should a title be translated exactly, or should it work well for the new audience?", "片名应该直译，还是应该让新的观众容易接受？"],
["lang", "超长的词", "Very long words", "Can you say \"Donaudampfschifffahrtsgesellschaft\"?", "你会说“Donaudampfschifffahrtsgesellschaft”吗？", "Make a new long German word by joining words together. What does it mean?", "把几个词拼在一起，造一个新的德语长词。它是什么意思？", "German builds long words, Chinese uses short characters, Portuguese has \"inconstitucionalissimamente\". Which language is the most efficient?", "德语造长词，中文用简短的汉字，葡萄牙语有“inconstitucionalissimamente”。哪种语言最高效？", "Are long words beautiful, practical or just funny?", "长词美、实用，还是只是好笑？"],
["lang", "奇怪的语法", "Strange grammar", "Which grammar rule do you hate?", "你最讨厌哪条语法规则？", "Explain a strange grammar rule in your language to us.", "给我们解释一条你语言里奇怪的语法规则。", "German verbs go to the end, Chinese has no verb tenses, Portuguese has a future subjunctive. Which language has the strangest grammar?", "德语动词要放到句尾，中文动词没有时态变化，葡萄牙语有将来虚拟式。哪种语言的语法最奇怪？", "Mark Twain said German grammar was \"awful\". Is any grammar really harder, or only different from what we know?", "马克·吐温说德语语法“可怕”。语法真的有难易之分，还是只是和我们熟悉的不同？"],
["lang", "名词的性别", "Gender of nouns", "How do you remember \"der\", \"die\" and \"das\"?", "你怎么记“der”、“die”和“das”？", "Tell us about a gender mistake that made people laugh.", "讲讲一次用错词性惹人发笑的经历。", "In German \"the girl\" is neutral, in Portuguese \"the sun\" is male but in German it's female. Chinese has no grammatical gender at all. Does gender change how we see things?", "德语里“女孩”是中性，葡萄牙语里“太阳”是阳性而德语里是阴性，中文根本没有语法性别。词的性别会改变我们看事物的方式吗？", "Would languages be easier without grammatical gender? What would we lose?", "没有语法性别，语言会更容易吗？我们会失去什么？"],
["lang", "语气词", "Little words with big feelings", "What do \"doch\", \"吧\" or \"né\" mean?", "“doch”、“吧”或“né”是什么意思？", "Say one sentence with and without \"吧\", \"mal\" or \"né\". How does the feeling change?", "说一句话，分别加和不加“吧”、“mal”或“né”。语气有什么变化？", "These little words are almost impossible to translate. How do learners ever master them?", "这些小词几乎没法翻译。学习者究竟怎样才能掌握它们？", "Without particles, does a language sound cold? What do they give to a conversation?", "没有语气词，一种语言会显得冷冰冰吗？它们给对话带来了什么？"],
["lang", "用外语做梦", "Dreaming in another language", "In which language do you think when you are alone?", "一个人的时候你用哪种语言思考？", "Tell us about the first time you dreamed in German or another language.", "讲讲你第一次用德语或其他语言做梦的经历。", "Many people say dreaming in a language means you have \"made it\". Do you agree?", "很多人说用一种语言做梦就说明你“学成了”。你同意吗？", "When you switch languages, do you switch personalities too?", "切换语言时，你的性格也会切换吗？"],
["lang", "双语孩子", "Bilingual children", "Which languages would you like your children to speak?", "你希望你的孩子会说哪些语言？", "Tell us a funny mix of languages you heard from a child.", "讲讲你从孩子嘴里听到的一句好笑的混合语言。", "Many children of Chinese or Brazilian parents in Germany stop speaking their parents' language. How can families keep it alive?", "在德国，很多中国或巴西父母的孩子不再说父母的语言了。家庭怎样才能让它延续？", "Is growing up with two languages a gift, a challenge, or both?", "在两种语言中长大是一种馈赠、一种挑战，还是两者兼有？"],
["lang", "人造语言", "Invented languages", "Did you have a secret language with friends as a child?", "小时候你和朋友有过秘密语言吗？", "Invent three words for a new language. What do they mean?", "为一门新语言发明三个词。它们是什么意思？", "Esperanto was made so everyone could talk easily. Why didn't it become a world language?", "世界语是为了让所有人都能轻松交流而创造的。它为什么没成为世界通用语？", "Is a language only real if a community speaks it? What makes a language alive?", "只有一个群体在说，一种语言才算真的吗？是什么让一种语言有生命？"],
["lang", "手语", "Sign language", "Can you sign \"hello\" or \"thank you\"?", "你会用手语说“你好”或“谢谢”吗？", "Have you ever seen a sign language interpreter? Where?", "你见过手语翻译吗？在哪？", "German, Chinese and Brazilian sign languages are all different. Why isn't there one sign language for the whole world?", "德国、中国和巴西的手语各不相同。为什么全世界没有统一的手语？", "Should every school teach some sign language? What would change?", "每所学校都应该教一些手语吗？会带来什么变化？"],
["lang", "缩写", "Abbreviations", "What do \"z.B.\", \"usw.\" or \"vc\" mean?", "“z.B.”、“usw.”或“vc”是什么意思？", "Tell us about an abbreviation that confused you.", "讲讲一个让你困惑的缩写。", "German offices love long abbreviations like \"GmbH\" and \"Kfz\". Why do some languages have so many?", "德国的办公室很爱用“GmbH”、“Kfz”这样的长缩写。为什么有些语言缩写那么多？", "Do abbreviations make communication faster, or do they exclude people who don't know them?", "缩写让沟通更快，还是把不懂的人排除在外了？"],
["lang", "写信", "Writing letters", "Do you still get postcards?", "你还收到明信片吗？", "Tell us about a letter you will never forget.", "讲讲一封你永远不会忘记的信。", "German has fixed formulas like \"Sehr geehrte Damen und Herren\", Chinese letters have their own polite rules. What is hard about writing letters in a foreign language?", "德语有“Sehr geehrte Damen und Herren”这样的固定套语，中文书信也有自己的礼节规矩。用外语写信难在哪里？", "Is a handwritten letter more meaningful than a message? Why?", "手写信比消息更有意义吗？为什么？"],
["lang", "礼貌用语", "Polite words", "Do you say \"please\" to your family?", "你会对家人说“请”吗？", "Tell us about a time someone seemed rude, but it was just a language difference.", "讲讲一次某人看起来很无礼，其实只是语言差异的经历。", "Germans say \"bitte\" a lot, Brazilians use many little friendly words, Chinese often show politeness with actions instead of words. What is polite where you come from?", "德国人常说“bitte”，巴西人用很多亲切的小词，中国人常用行动而不是言语表达礼貌。在你的家乡，什么算礼貌？", "Can you be too polite? When does politeness feel cold?", "会不会太客气了？什么时候礼貌会让人觉得冷淡？"],
["lang", "冷知识", "Fun facts", "Tell us a fun fact about your hometown or country.", "讲一个关于你家乡或国家的冷知识。", "Share the strangest fact you learned this year.", "分享你今年学到的最奇怪的知识。", "Germany has over 1,500 kinds of sausage. China eats half of the world's pork. Brazil has more frogs than any other country. Which fact surprises you most?", "德国有一千五百多种香肠，中国吃掉了世界一半的猪肉，巴西的青蛙种类比任何国家都多。哪个事实最让你吃惊？", "Why do we love useless facts so much?", "为什么我们那么喜欢没用的知识？"],
["lang", "背单词", "Learning vocabulary", "Flashcards, apps, songs or sticky notes on the fridge?", "单词卡、App、唱歌，还是贴在冰箱上的便利贴？", "Tell us about a word you could never remember, and how you finally learned it.", "讲讲一个你怎么也记不住的词，以及你最后是怎么记住的。", "Some people learn 20 words a day, others learn by living in the language. Which works better for you?", "有人一天背二十个词，有人通过在语言环境中生活来学。哪种对你更有效？", "How many words do you need to really \"speak\" a language?", "要真正“会说”一门语言，需要多少词汇？"],
["lang", "颜色俗语", "Colour expressions", "Do you know expressions with colours in your language?", "你知道你语言里带颜色的俗语吗？", "Explain a colour expression from your language.", "解释一句你语言里带颜色的俗语。", "In German you can be \"blue\" (drunk), in English \"blue\" (sad), in Chinese \"red\" means popular. Why do colours mean such different things?", "德语里“blau”是喝醉了，英语里“blue”是难过，中文里“红”表示受欢迎。为什么颜色的含义差别这么大？", "Can you translate a colour expression word for word? What happens?", "你能逐字翻译一句颜色俗语吗？会怎样？"],
["lang", "天气俗语", "Weather sayings", "Do you know a weather saying, like \"April does what it wants\"?", "你知道什么天气俗语吗？比如“四月想怎样就怎样”？", "Explain a weather saying from your country. Is it true?", "解释一句你们国家的天气俗语。它是真的吗？", "English has \"raining cats and dogs\", German \"es gießt in Strömen\", Portuguese \"chover canivetes\". Which picture do you like best?", "英语说“下猫下狗”，德语说“雨像河流一样倒下来”，葡萄牙语说“下小刀”。你最喜欢哪个画面？", "Why is weather the safest topic for small talk everywhere?", "为什么在世界各地，天气都是闲聊最安全的话题？"],
["lang", "食物俗语", "Food expressions", "Which food appears most in sayings in your language?", "在你的语言里，哪种食物最常出现在俗语中？", "Explain a food expression, like \"Das ist nicht mein Bier\" or \"吃醋\".", "解释一句食物俗语，比如“Das ist nicht mein Bier”（不是我的啤酒）或“吃醋”。", "German says \"everything has an end, only the sausage has two\", Brazilians \"spill the broth\", Chinese \"eat vinegar\" when jealous. Why do so many languages use food to talk about life?", "德语说“万物都有一个尽头，只有香肠有两个”，巴西人说“把汤洒了”，中国人吃醋时说“吃醋”。为什么那么多语言用食物来谈人生？", "What does a culture's food language say about what matters to it?", "一种文化的食物语言说明了它重视什么？"],
["lang", "最难的语言", "The hardest language", "How many languages do you speak?", "你会说几种语言？", "Tell us about the hardest moment in learning a language.", "讲讲学语言时最难的时刻。", "People say Chinese is hardest for Germans and German hardest for Brazilians. Is there really a \"hardest\" language, or does it depend on where you start?", "有人说对德国人来说中文最难，对巴西人来说德语最难。真的有“最难”的语言吗？还是取决于你的起点？", "What keeps you going when learning a language gets hard?", "学语言变难的时候，是什么让你坚持下去？"],
["lang", "自言自语", "Talking to yourself", "In which language do you talk to yourself?", "你用哪种语言自言自语？", "Tell us about a time someone caught you talking to yourself.", "讲讲一次你自言自语被人撞见的经历。", "Some learners practise a language by talking to themselves. Have you tried it?", "有些学习者通过自言自语来练语言。你试过吗？", "What is the voice in your head like? Is it kind or strict?", "你脑海里的声音是什么样的？温和还是严厉？"],
["lang", "故事接龙", "Story chain", "Let's start: \"Once upon a time, there was a cat who...\" Everyone adds one sentence!", "开始吧：“从前有一只猫，它……”每人加一句！", "Continue the story with a surprise: something nobody expects.", "用一个惊喜继续故事：发生一件没人预料到的事。", "Now tell the story from the cat's point of view. What changes?", "现在从猫的角度讲这个故事。有什么变化？", "Why do humans tell stories? What would we be without them?", "人类为什么讲故事？没有故事我们会怎样？"],
["lang", "二选一", "This or that?", "Mountains or sea? Cats or dogs? Morning or night?", "山还是海？猫还是狗？早上还是晚上？", "Make your own \"this or that\" question for the group and explain your answer.", "给大家出一道你自己的二选一题，并说说你的答案。", "Would you rather speak every language or play every instrument?", "你宁愿会说所有语言，还是会演奏所有乐器？", "Do quick choices show who we really are, or just our mood today?", "快速的选择能显示我们真正是谁，还是只是今天的心情？"],
["lang", "一个词形容", "One word to describe it", "Describe your hometown in one word.", "用一个词形容你的家乡。", "Choose one word for each person here, and explain why.", "给在座的每个人选一个词，并说明原因。", "Describe your country in one word, then ask someone from another country to do the same. Do you agree?", "用一个词形容你的国家，再请来自其他国家的人也形容一下。你同意吗？", "Can one word ever be enough? What gets lost when we simplify?", "一个词真的够吗？简化时我们失去了什么？"]
